    <section>
        <h2>XY-Plane</h2>
        <p>XY-plane can be described using vectors.  </p>
        <ul>
            <li>The unit vector {`\\(\\hat{i}\\)`} points along the direction of positive {`\\(x\\)`}-axis.</li>
            <li>The unit vector {`\\(\\hat{j}\\)`} points along the direction of positive {`\\(y\\)`}-axis.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Notice that the angle between {`\\(\\hat{i}\\)`} and {`\\(\\hat{j}\\)`} is {`\\(90^\\circ\\)`}. The XY-plane can be seen as a collection of points (say P) written as {`\\((x, y)\\)`} where {`\\(x\\)`} distance along the {`\\(x\\)`}-axis and {`\\(y\\)`} is the distance along the {`\\(y\\)`}-axis. Let O be the origin at {`\\((0, 0)\\)`}. Draw an arrow from O to P. This arrow is a vector representing the point P in the XY-plane.</p>
